# rooms.pdl - the floating-island town (BOOK 16.game/EDIT-ISLANDS-DESIGN.md). Every room is an "over" room here: cols x rows cells of tile_px (24), no wall strip; what is solid, where the doors are and how the
# rooms are painted comes from the skin (ops/rpg_edit_hq.c builds the island map and the interiors, the doors are the D cells of the island map), not from SCENERY / DOOR rows.
# ROOM | id | name | floor_col | floor_row | over | cols | rows | tile_px | biome      floor_col,floor_row = the Inside_A5 floor tile of an interior (island: unused)
# The interiors are named after the building of the door that leads to them, in the order the doors are found on the map (top to bottom, left to right).
ROOM | start  | Islands | 0 | 0 | over | 56 | 17 | 24 | islands
ROOM | bank   | Bank    | 1 | 4 | over | 24 | 17 | 24 | interior
ROOM | store  | Store   | 1 | 2 | over | 24 | 17 | 24 | interior
ROOM | hotel  | Hotel   | 3 | 4 | over | 24 | 17 | 24 | interior
ROOM | school | School  | 5 | 4 | over | 24 | 17 | 24 | interior
ROOM | cabin  | Cabin   | 0 | 2 | over | 24 | 17 | 24 | interior
